course: dictionary
lesson: 15613
title: Tartaric
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tartaric is a science and cooking word. It describes tartaric acid, a natural acid found in grapes, bananas and tamarinds. «Tartaric acid is found in grapes.» Here tartaric tells you which kind of acid it is.
explain: Use the context clues. The sentence names grapes, bananas and tamarinds, which are foods, so tartaric acid must be an acid found in food. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A food acid fits, but a colour or a sport does not.
explain: Tartaric acid is used in cooking. «Mum added cream of tartar so the egg whites would whip up fluffy.» Cream of tartar is made from tartaric acid, and tartaric acid is also used in baking powder and in making wine.
fact: Tartaric is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as tartaric acid.
fact: Tartaric acid is a natural acid found in grapes, bananas and tamarinds.
fact: Tartaric acid is a safe food acid, so it is used in cooking.
fact: «Cream of tartar» helps egg whites whip, and it is made from tartaric acid.
fact: Tartaric acid is used in baking powder and in making wine.
exercise: «Tartaric acid is found in grapes, bananas and tamarinds.» What kind of acid is tartaric acid? | *A natural acid found in food | A kind of cloud over the sea | A metal that rusts in the rain
exercise: Mum says, «Add a pinch of cream of tartar to the egg whites.» Why does she use it? | *It helps the egg whites whip up fluffy | It makes the eggs turn blue | It stops the oven getting hot
exercise: «Tartaric acid is found in grapes, bananas and tamarinds.» Which of these is a fruit that tartaric acid is found in? | Snow | Rocks | Sand | *Bananas
test: «The fizzy sherbet bubbled when the tartaric acid mixed with bicarbonate of soda.» What did the tartaric acid mix with? | Milk | Sugar | Water | *Bicarbonate of soda
test: What is tartaric acid used for in cooking? | Making wire | Lighting fires | Painting walls | *Baking powder
exam: «Cream of tartar» is made from which acid? | Sugar | Milk | Salt | *Tartaric acid
